    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_342059f405b930ee0c359b95dfd43301485e8047c6bd4504af5ed631accec7f7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source has a layered dependency structure rather than one uniform proof chain. Lemmas 1 and 2 establish finiteness and individual-horizon asymptotics; Conjecture 1 is still needed to obtain the global survival theorem, and Conjecture 3 is additionally needed to reduce correlations to collision-free horizon integrals for the superdiffusion theorem. Simulations test selected survival consequences, while the critical-dimension and RH discussions add separate heuristic or analytic assumptions that those figures do not discharge.",
