    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3fabcab38e087f2b553bd7475ab5c6f1318c315f4e517117129b44d92e657bb0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Enumerating principal horizons by primitive dual-lattice vectors creates the arithmetic entry point: Möbius inversion removes primitivity and inserts 1/zeta(s+1) into the Mellin integrand. Residues then translate zeta-zero locations into small-scatterer powers, and the survival-to-diffusion relation carries the same formal RH-sensitive remainder into the superdiffusion coefficient.",
