    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c26169298bf4ce7cc636b4c9fb8923fdb712fa1364df55a6061208de547c1d19",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Horizon codimension links collision-free geometry to transport scaling. A non-incipient horizon of dimension d_H contributes F_H(t) proportional to t^{-(d-d_H)}; if maximal horizons dominate total survival and colliding trajectories decorrelate below that scale, only codimension-one principal horizons sustain a 1/t velocity-correlation term and hence logarithmic superdiffusion.",
