    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d626423ea4262a77f6f93fd3a7fae80eb314db176305158ecc05ca28925a1ac3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "In logarithmic superdiffusion, weak convergence and second-moment normalization sample different parts of the displacement law: the scaled Gaussian core carries covariance Xi, while finite-time ballistic tails can vanish from the weak limit yet supply the remaining leading-order contribution to the logarithmic second moment. For the corridor Lorentz gas, the source therefore proposes Xi=D rather than the ordinary-diffusion relation Xi=2D.",
